 in the 1908 earthquake and was restored between 1919 and 1920. During the Second World War, Allied bombings destroyed part of the Cathedral, which was rebuilt in 1943. It is consecrated to the “ Virgin of the L"},{"name":"Astronomical clock in Messina","local":"Orologio astronomico di Messina","wd":"Q546826","lat":38.1923,"lng":15.5547,"sl":9,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikidata (Wikipedia in many languages)","Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"The Duomo's bell tower has one of the largest astronomical clocks in the world, built in 1933 by the Ungerer Company of Strasbourg. A must-see for visitors with an amazing clock show, including symbolical and allegorical moving metal animals and statues, every day at 12:00."},{"name":"Church of the Santissima Annunziata dei Catalani","local":"Chiesa della Santissima Annunziata dei Catalani","wd":"Q3669197","lat":38.19123,"lng":15.55638,"sl":8,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikidata (Wikipedia in many languages)","Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"One of a few survivors of the earthquake in 1908. Its origin dates to the 12th century in later Norman style with Arabic-influenced elements."},{"name":"Fountain of Orion","local":"Fontana di Orione","wd":"Q3747419","lat":38.19227,"lng":15.55428,"sl":5,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Work of Montorsoli (1547), a student of Michelangelo. Orion, with his dog Sirius, is portrayed as one of the legendary founders of Messina."},{"name":"Regional museum of Messina","local":"Museo Regionale Interdisciplinare di Messina (MuMe)","wd":"Q1526140","lat":38.21718,"lng":15.56438,"sl":5,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Collections of medieval art and modern works. Note especially the altarpiece of San Gregorio by Antonello da Messina, and the Resurrezione di Lazzaro (Raising of Lazarus) and Adorazione dei pastori (Adoration of the Shepherds) both by Caravaggio."},{"name":"Santa Maria Alemanna","local":"Chiesa di Santa Maria Alemanna","wd":"Q3673236","lat":38.18832,"lng":15.55683,"sl":3,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"This former church built early 13th century is a rare example of a Gothic style in the city. The church was badly damaged in 1908 and was open back to the public in 2001. It hosts various exhibitions."},{"name":"Fountain of Neptune","local":"Fontana del Nettuno","wd":"Q3747360","lat":38.19937,"lng":15.55777,"sl":3,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Another monumental fountain by Montorsoli featuring Neptune accompanied with Scylla and Charybdis."},{"name":"Palazzo Zanca","wd":"Q3891107","lat":38.19397,"lng":15.5557,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Municipio of Messina was built in 1924 in Neoclassical style under direction by Antonio Zanca."},{"name":"Quattro Fontane","wd":"Q28669612","lat":38.19074,"lng":15.55587,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Two smaller fountains survived out of four built between 1666 and 1742."},{"name":"Forte Gonzaga","wd":"Q13196191","lat":38.1881,"lng":15.54083,"sl":8,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikidata (Wikipedia in many languages)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Statue of John of Austria","local":"Statua di don Giovanni d'Austria","wd":"Q3968667","lat":38.19136,"lng":15.5558,"sl":6,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Palazzo del Monte di Pietà","wd":"Q1423732","lat":38.19481,"lng":15.55263,"sl":5,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"The current building is essentially a ground floor of the former palazzo which was severely damaged by earthquakes and World War II bombing."},{"name":"Forte del Santissimo Salvatore","wd":"Q3748665","lat":38.19708,"lng":15.56432,"sl":5,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Galleria Vittorio Emanuele III","wd":"Q3094793","lat":38.19425,"lng":15.55395,"sl":4,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"An eclectic building constructed between 1924 and 1929 in Liberty style. Inside it consists of 3 passages converging into a hexagonal centre covered by a glass dome. It's somewhat similar to other galleria's across Italy."},{"name":"Palazzo della cultura","wd":"Q3891490","lat":38.1975,"lng":15.55376,"sl":4,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Madonna della Lettera","wd":"Q3842666","lat":38.19653,"lng":15.56278,"sl":3,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"The Madonna of the Letter is venerated by the Catholic Church as a saint patron of Messina. A towering gilded statue of the Madonna della Lettera is located atop of the tall Forte San Salvatore tower at the tip of the sickle in the sickle-shaped harbour. The inscription \"We bless you and your City\" "},{"name":"Real Cittadella","wd":"Q3930982","lat":38.20304,"lng":15.55582,"sl":3,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"The former main gate of the Messina's citadel. These days it stays at the Piazza Casa Pia dei Poveri. A few other surviving parts of the citadel still can be seen at the original location of the citadel at the SE corner of the port albeit in a pretty neglected state."},{"name":"Monumental Cemetery of Messina","local":"Cimitero monumentale di Messina","wd":"Q3676893","lat":38.1758,"lng":15.541,"sl":3,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Palazzo Calapaj - d'Alcontres","local":"Palazzo Calapaj-d'Alcontres","wd":"Q3889746","lat":38.19184,"lng":15.5555,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"An 18th-century building, perhaps of a relatively modest exterior, but it's one of a few ones survived the earthquake of 1908."},{"name":"Santa Maria di Montalto","local":"Santuario della Madonna di Montalto","wd":"Q3949829","lat":38.19357,"lng":15.55076,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"Sanctuary is a building made in an eclectic style with Gothic and Romanesque elements, located high above the Piazza del Duomo. From its lookout point, with a statue of the Pope admiring the view, you can enjoy a panorama of the Messina harbour and the Strait of Messina."},{"name":"Sant'Eustochia","local":"Chiesa di Montevergine","wd":"Q28669610","lat":38.19594,"lng":15.55321,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":false,"src":["Wikivoyage (English)","Wikivoyage (Italian)","Wikipedia in Italian"],"en":"The church hosts remains of the Catholic saint Eustochia Smeralda Calafato."},{"name":"Falconieri fountain","local":"Fontana Falconieri","wd":"Q48806154","lat":38.19468,"lng":15.55105,"sl":2,"unesco":false,"heritage":true,"src":["Wikivoyage (Italian)","national heritage register","Wikipedia in Italian"]},{"name":"Fountain of Gennaro","local":"Fontana di Gennaro","wd":"Q3747417","